 "caveats": [
  "Small sample (21 queries, 68 directed positives): read the bootstrap intervals, not the point estimates.",
  "The news feature is built from keyword weights curated by the same author as the documented edges; its strong baseline performance may reflect curation leakage rather than independent signal.",
  "Ties are broken by seeded random shuffles averaged over several trials (deterministic, not exact ranks).",
  "Reference variants (zero-fill, shrinkage) are analysis aids only; the application does not use them.",
  "'Hard negatives' are issuers with NO DOCUMENTED edge to the query. The edge list is curated and incomplete, so undocumented is not proven unrelated.",
  "The composite measures SIMILARITY (sector, geography, text, themes); the documented edges are supply/licence DEPENDENCIES. With the edges masked, ranking dependencies by similarity is a hard task by construction - a low score here says the composite is not a dependency detector, not that the similarity it computes is wrong.",
  "The 34 expert anchors are easy (a supplier vs an oil major): single features score 94-100% on them, so they cannot tell weight sets apart, and the existing train/holdout split shares entities."
